## Use the package

- **Place a figure in a report or application.** Use the PDF for print and the PNG for Word or slides. Alt text for each figure is in `docs/figure_notes.md`.
- **Edit in QGIS.** Install the fonts, then open `qgis/{{ p.id }}.qgz`. See `qgis/README.md`.
- **Edit in ArcGIS Pro.** Copy this folder to a short local path such as `C:\GIS\{{ p.id }}`, install the fonts, add `arcgis/Build_Maps.pyt` as a toolbox and run **Build project and layouts**. See `arcgis/README.md`.
- **Edit in Illustrator.** Install the fonts and run `illustrator/Open_Maps_In_Illustrator.jsx`. See `illustrator/README.md`.
- **View in Google Earth.** Open `google-earth/{{ p.id }}.kmz`.

